cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the BDR software, cite this software release and the associated scientific preprint where appropriate."
title: "Banco de Dados Resolutivo (BDR) / Resolutive Database Engine"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-09
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Matos"
    given-names: "Marcelo Roldão"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6075-4680"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-DB"
url: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-DB"
abstract: >-
  BDR is an experimental persistent key-value database research project investigating
  deterministic resolutive addressing, local partitioning, adaptive data structures,
  write-ahead logging, atomic checkpoints, crash recovery, and reproducible performance
  evaluation. Version 0.1.0 is a Research Preview and does not claim production readiness
  or strict worst-case O(1) complexity for the complete engine.
keywords:
  - resolutive database
  - key-value database
  - persistent storage
  - write-ahead log
  - crash recovery
  - adaptive partitioning
  - benchmarking
  - reproducible research
